{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558297-rage-across-anatolia-an-unofficial-savage-age-document","id":1558297,"title":"Rage Across Anatolia - An unofficial Savage Age document","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-13T15:49:43-08:00","id":1558297,"title":"Rage Across Anatolia - An unofficial Savage Age document","content":"So i have recently completed working on a document fleshing out Anatolia in 23,000 BC at the start of the Savage Age period. This is not an official Savage Age product, just something i have done to make running Savage Age games myself that i thought others might find useful.<br /> <br /> it is over 100 pages, has around 75 stated out Fera NPCs, about 40 locations detailed and just shy of 20 generic human and Fera statlines. And there are a bunch of basic maps showing where all the locations are in Anatolia. You will need some Savage Age books to get full use out of the named NPCs as many of them use gifts, fetishes and totems from those books.<br /> <br /> if you find an error please let me know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NfNLvc8Ru7dlWorB5EEAefU9zjm3V5rJEDDMPBgJxjQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NfNLvc8Ru7dlWorB5EEAefU9zjm3V5rJEDDMPBgJxjQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NfNLvc8Ru7dlWorB5EEAefU9zjm3V5rJEDDMPBgJxjQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/documen